1
00:05:15,789 --> 00:05:21,789
Not man. Not machine. More.

2
00:10:31,578 --> 00:10:37,578
Upgrade is a action, thriller, science fiction film directed by Leigh Whannell.

3
00:15:47,368 --> 00:15:53,368
A brutal mugging leaves Grey Trace paralyzed in the
hospital and his beloved wife dead.

4
00:21:03,157 --> 00:21:09,157
A billionaire inventor soon offers Trace a cure — an artificial
intelligence implant called STEM that will enhance his body.

5
00:26:18,947 --> 00:26:24,947
Now able to walk, Grey finds that he also has superhuman strength and agility —
skills he uses to seek revenge against the thugs who destroyed his life.

6
00:31:34,736 --> 00:31:40,736
Grey Trace, played by Logan Marshall-Green.

7
00:36:50,526 --> 00:36:56,526
Detective Cortez, played by Betty Gabriel.

8
00:42:06,315 --> 00:42:12,315
Eron Keen, played by Harrison Gilbertson.

9
00:47:22,105 --> 00:47:28,105
Asha Trace, played by Melanie Vallejo.

10
00:52:37,894 --> 00:52:43,894
Fisk, played by Benedict Hardie.

11
00:57:53,684 --> 00:57:59,684
Pamela, played by Linda Cropper.

12
01:03:09,473 --> 01:03:15,473
Upgrade is a 2018 cyberpunk action horror film written and directed by Leigh Whannell,
and starring Logan Marshall-Green, Betty Gabriel, and Harrison Gilbertson.

13
01:08:25,263 --> 01:08:31,263
Upgrade follows a technophobe who is implanted with a chip that allows him
to control his body after a mugging left him paralyzed.

14
01:13:41,052 --> 01:13:47,052
The film was produced by Jason Blum, under his Blumhouse Productions banner.

15
01:18:56,842 --> 01:19:02,842
After premiering on 10 March 2018 at South by Southwest, Upgrade was released on 1 June 2018 in
the United States by OTL Releasing and Blumhouse Tilt, and on 14 June in Australia.

16
01:24:12,631 --> 01:24:18,631
The film made $17 million on a $3 million budget and received positive reviews from critics, who called it "one part The Six
Million Dollar Man, one part Death Wish revenge fantasy", and praised its dark humor and action sequences.

17
01:29:28,421 --> 01:29:34,421
The film explores themes of future, artificial
intelligence (a.i.), hacker, police, technology.

18
01:34:44,210 --> 01:34:50,210
The tone is dark and thought_provoking and intense.
